            <ArticleTitle>Headache in acromegaly: dramatic improvement with the somatostatin analogue SMS 201-995.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two acromegalic patients with severe headache, persisting after pituitary adenomectomy followed by radiotherapy in one, were treated with the somatostatin analogue SMS 201-995. Both had been resistant to conventional headache therapy and experienced dramatic and rapid relief after the first injection of the analogue. This result persisted with long-term treatment of the drug. Although the mechanism of action of SMS 201-995 in pain remains unclear, the rapid and efficacious analgesic effect of this compound may be one more indication for its use in pituitary tumors associated with cephalalgias.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
